I was cleaning up the main dungeon before heading into Gehennom, and at
the bottom of the Gnomish Mines I momentarily encountered my original dog,
which had gotten separated from me way back when (given that it's now
roughly turn 170,000, it must have been over 100,000 turns ago).
Obviously, there is no way to save a pet under such a circumstance; I got
the "You feel worried about Triskele" message the instant I came down the
stairs, and immediately teleported over to him (I normally travel
blindfolded, now that green slime has been genocided - with 702 HP, and
everything erodeproofed, there's not much else I can blunder into that
will be of concern), only to watch him turn into a corpse before my eyes.
This I simply take as part of the game.
However, while pondering the tragic nature of the game keeping that poor
digital dog alive but starving, alone, for over 100K turns, it occurred to
me that surely, SURELY players have managed to keep their original
starting pet alive for the entire game, and ascended with them in tow. But
I've never seen this mentioned as a possible "conduct" to keep track of.
Is there no way for the game to give you a special message when a pet that
is ascending with you is your starting pet? If treated as a conduct, would
it not be possible to have the game tell you "Your starting pet was still
alive" when the game ends? Or would this odd program quirk (where the game
keeps pets alive in limbo indefinitely when they're stranded on an
unvisited level) screw that up?

